                                        <height>190</height>
                                        <width>162</width>
                                    </dimensions><dimensions subtype="computed" unit="mm" type="outer"><height quantity="190" unit="mm"/><width quantity="162" unit="mm"/></dimensions>
                                </extent>
                                <foliation/>
                                <collation>
                                    <signatures>
                                        Quires marks are indicated on the inner upper and lower corners of the first folio of quires 2-7, and on the lower corner of the first folio of quires 8-13. 
                                        Quire marks are decorated: those of quires 2-6 are written in the main hand and surrounded by four dots; 
                                        those of quires 7-13 are smaller in size and are surrounded by single thin lines. 
                                    </signatures>
                                    <note>
                                        According to the catalogue, the manuscript consists of 14 quires, which are all quaternions, except the seventh (which is a quinion), the last-but-one (which is a ternion) and the last one (which is a binion). This description only adds up to 106 folios assuming that <foreign xml:lang="la">‘binionem’</foreign> is a typo for <foreign xml:lang="la">‘bifolium’</foreign>.
                                    </note>
                                </collation>
                                <condition key="good">
                                    <locus target="#106"/> is torn, with loss of text. The outer edge of the textblock is trimmed.                                    
                                </condition>
                            </supportDesc>
                            
                            <layoutDesc>                             
                                <layout columns="2" writtenLines="20">     
                                </layout><layout subtype="computed" type="catalogue" columns="2"><writtenLines quantity="20"/></layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                       
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                                <seg type="script">18th-century script</seg>
                                <date notBefore="1700" notAfter="1799"/>      
                                <seg type="ink">Black, red</seg>
                                <desc>
                                    Some paleographic features:
                                    the upper parts of ቆ, ቶ, የ, ደ and ጸ have angular shape;
                                    ዐ has angular shape;
                                    ጵ has the ancient shape on <locus target="#51"/>, with the vowel marker on the upper left part of the letter.
                                </desc>
                                <seg type="rubrication">Headings.</seg>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                        
                        <additions>
                            <list>
                                <item xml:id="e1">                                    
                                    <desc>Few words of a confession of faith are written on <locus target="106v"/>.</desc>
                                </item>
                                <item xml:id="e2">
                                    <desc>Few corrections over erasure and in the margins.</desc>
                                </item>
                                <item xml:id="e3">
                                    <desc>The first word of quires 3-7 is also written on the inner lower corner of the last folios of the previous quires.</desc>
                                </item>
                            </list>
                        </additions>
                        
